BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Linda Linda Linda
DTSTART:20250920T013000Z
DTEND:20250920T034500Z
DTSTAMP:20250920T013000Z
UID:qOBp9MVEPx
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 114 mins (1h54m)\n\nDays before a crucial festival a
 ppearance\, aspiring teenage rock stars Kyoko and Nozomi find themselves w
 ithout a band when their guitarist injures her finger and their singer qui
 ts. Now\, their only chance for superstardom lies in a new vocalist who ha
 s never been in a band and barely speaks Japanese. Linda Linda Linda is a 
 hidden gem of Japanese cinema that has gained a cult following despite its
  limited U.S. release. Featuring music by James Iha (The Smashing Pumpkins
 ). New 4K restoration in celebration of its 20th anniversary.\n\nhttps://
 www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/linda-linda-linda-20th-anniversary
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Color of Pomegranates
DTSTART:20250920T190000Z
DTEND:20250920T204000Z
DTSTAMP:20250920T190000Z
UID:j4lJ45kvr9
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 77 mins (1h17m)\n\nKino Armenia Sergei Parajanov’s
  empirical masterpiece loosely follows the life of Sayat Nova\, “King of
  Song\,” an Armenian poet and musician born in the 18th century\, throug
 h vibrant sets and costumes and hypnotic shots. This colorful and avant-ga
 rde masterpiece provides an utterly transformative cinematic experience.\n
 \nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/education/adult-film-education/
 kino-armenia/the-color-of-pomegranates
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
